## Ingredients

- 3–4 lbs Lean Ground Beef  
- 2 Yellow Onions (diced)  
- 1 Bunch of Fresh Cilantro (chopped)  
- 2 Med Cans or 4 Fresh Green Chilis  
- 2 Large Cans Red Enchilada Sauce  
- 2 Packs Large Tortillas  
- 1 Large Bag Fiesta Blend Cheese  
- Sour Cream  

### Seasonings (all to taste)

- Adobo Seasoning  
- Garlic Salt  
- Onion Powder  
- Celery Salt  
- Cayenne Pepper  
- Cumin  
- Salt & Pepper  

## Directions

1. Preheat your oven to 350°F.  
2. While the oven is preheating, start cooking the ground beef.  
3. When the beef is about halfway done, add the diced onions, green chilis, spices, and some chopped cilantro. Finish cooking the meat and then drain.  
4. Pour enough enchilada sauce into the bottom of your baking dish to cover with about a fingertip’s depth.  
5. To assemble each enchilada:  
   - Lay out a tortilla.  
   - Spoon some enchilada sauce into the center and spread it towards the edges (about halfway).  
   - Add a generous line of the meat mixture.  
   - Drizzle a bit more sauce over the meat.  
   - Sprinkle with cheese and cilantro.  
   - Roll up the tortilla and place it seam-side down in the baking dish.  
6. Repeat until you’ve filled the dish or used up your tortillas.  
7. Pour the remaining enchilada sauce over the top, then sprinkle with the remaining cheese and cilantro.  
8. Bake at 350°F for 35–40 minutes (times and temps may vary).  
9. Let cool for 10 minutes, then serve with extra cilantro and sour cream.
